  ],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Let's compare both methods.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 1560,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 47,
      "word_count": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "Method one, direction simulation with visited takes OM times N time and OM times N auxiliary space.",
      "start_ms": 2380,
      "end_ms": 11160,
      "start_frame": 71,
      "end_frame": 335,
      "word_count": 17
    },
    {
      "text": "Method two, shrinking boundaries also takes OM times N time, but only O1 auxiliary space.",
      "start_ms": 11880,
      "end_ms": 20840,
      "start_frame": 356,
      "end_frame": 625,
      "word_count": 15
    },
    {
      "text": "So the optimization is not about time.",
      "start_ms": 21600,
      "end_ms": 23720,
      "start_frame": 648,
      "end_frame": 712,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "The improvement is how we represent the remaining work.",
      "start_ms": 24180,
      "end_ms": 27220,
      "start_frame": 725,
      "end_frame": 817,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "Now remember these important mistakes.",
      "start_ms": 27620,
      "end_ms": 29880,
      "start_frame": 829,
      "end_frame": 896,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "First, do not assume the matrix is square.",
      "start_ms": 30520,
      "end_ms": 33180,
      "start_frame": 916,
      "end_frame": 995,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "It is M by N, rows and columns can be different.",
      "start_ms": 33560,
      "end_ms": 37380,
      "start_frame": 1007,
      "end_frame": 1121,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "Second, in method one, do not turn only at the border.",
      "start_ms": 37820,
      "end_ms": 42080,
      "start_frame": 1135,
      "end_frame": 1262,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "You must turn when the next cell is outside or already visited.",
      "start_ms": 42560,
      "end_ms": 47340,
      "start_frame": 1277,
      "end_frame": 1420,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "Third, in the boundary method, consume an edge first, then shrink its boundary.",
      "start_ms": 48320,
      "end_ms": 54580,
      "start_frame": 1450,
      "end_frame": 1637,
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "Do not shrink before processing it.",
      "start_ms": 54780,
      "end_ms": 57680,
      "start_frame": 1643,
      "end_frame": 1730,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "Fourth, after shrinking, validate the remaining rectangle before processing another edge.",
      "start_ms": 57700,
      "end_ms": 63820,
      "start_frame": 1731,
      "end_frame": 1915,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "Otherwise, single row and single column cases can create duplicate values.",
      "start_ms": 64440,
      "end_ms": 70460,
      "start_frame": 1933,
      "end_frame": 2114,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "And finally, do not stop just because only one row or one column is left.",
      "start_ms": 71360,
      "end_ms": 78200,
      "start_frame": 2141,
      "end_frame": 2346,
      "word_count": 15
    },
    {
      "text": "Those cells are still valid work.",
      "start_ms": 78680,
      "end_ms": 80760,
      "start_frame": 2360,
      "end_frame": 2423,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "So the same logic handles a one by one matrix, a single row, a single column, wide matrices and tall matrices.",
      "start_ms": 80760,
      "end_ms": 90680,
      "start_frame": 2423,
      "end_frame": 2720,
      "word_count": 21
    },
    {
      "text": "Duplicate values, negative values and zeros also change nothing because our traversal depends on positions, not on the values stored there.",
      "start_ms": 91500,
      "end_ms": 105840,
      "start_frame": 2745,
      "end_frame": 3175,
      "word_count": 21
    }
  ],
